// Tabs and wide characters on one line, which is where the two rules have to
// agree. A tab is ONE column (the compiler cannot know the reader's tab
// width) and is echoed as a single space, so it contributes one cell as well
// as one column; the ideographs after it contribute two cells each and one
// column each. The line below is indented with one real tab.
if (true) {
	print("組" + nope);
}
